# v1.14 — retrain both defend scenarios under the horizon criterion.
#
# DEFEND success is now conservation of the position to a stated hour, not
# annihilation of the enemy (eccf816). Phase 2 established what the change is
# worth as a RE-SCORING: on the committed checkpoints, at horizon =
# int(0.5 * max_steps), N=100 seed 123, ckpt_latest, the criterion reproduces
# the offline reference exactly — defend_brique_v9 91 -> 88, v10 88 -> 99,
# v6 97 -> 99.
#
# That is a statement about the scoring rule and NOT about the policies. These
# two runs are what separates the claims: same scenarios, same budgets, same
# seed and the same `defend_survivor_scale=0.35` as the runs they replace
# (fireteam_defend_v15, defend_brique_v9), so the criterion — and the DONE
# channel it reopens to the root — is the only variable.
fireteam_defend_v16  --scenario fireteam_defend --total-steps 3500000 --seed 12 --reward defend_survivor_scale=0.35
defend_brique_v11    --scenario defend_brique   --total-steps 3000000 --seed 12 --reward defend_survivor_scale=0.35
